 "translation": "But later, \"Of the Toba Tek Singh Government\" took the place of \"Of the Pakistan Government,\" and he began asking other lunatics where Toba Tek Singh, the place he belonged to, was. But no one knew whether it was in Pakistan or Hindustan. Those who tried to explain would get entangled in the confusion that Sialkot was first in Hindustan, but now it's heard to be in Pakistan. Who knows if Lahore, which is in Pakistan today, might go to Hindustan tomorrow, or if all of Hindustan might become Pakistan? And who could say with certainty that both Hindustan and Pakistan might not disappear completely one day?",
